\details{
\strong{Variance SEs and MLS statuses.} For balanced ANOVA map \code{theta = A \%*\% MS},
unbiased sampling covariance is \code{A \%*\% diag(2 * MS^2 / (df + 2)) \%*\% t(A)}
(urGENOVA SEVC convention). Ting et al. (1990) MLS intervals retain
unrestricted \code{RawLower}/\code{RawUpper} and intersect \code{Lower}/\code{Upper} with
\verb{[0, Inf)}, distinguishing \code{"Available"}, \code{"Includes zero"}, \code{"Empty nonnegative interval"}, \code{"Degenerate mean squares"}, \code{"Numerical interval failure"}, and \code{"Variance interval below numeric resolution"}.

\strong{Between-score covariances and incomplete sources.} Signed covariance
intervals are never truncated at zero. For Wishart blocks \code{nu * S} (\code{nu > 1}),
elementwise unbiased variance is \code{(nu*x*y + (nu - 2)*c^2) / ((nu - 1)*(nu + 2))}; \code{"gci"} propagates Bartlett pivots \code{nu*(c - sqrt(x*y - c^2)*Z / sqrt(U2)) / U1} (Krishnamoorthy & Xia, 2007), while \code{"regression_region"}
encloses regression-slope \code{t} and predictor chi-square pivots at block level
\code{level^(1/K)} (using Cauchy-Schwarz on \code{df = 1} or singular blocks).
\code{"reml_profile"} and \code{"residual_contrast"} retain original ANOVA/MINQUE
\code{Estimate} alongside separate \code{IntervalCenter} (\code{SE = NA}); finite-sample
interval precision depends on block degrees of freedom and cell balance.

Rows and columns refer to \strong{estimated components}, such as Person, Task
and Residual. This is neither the covariance matrix between individual
ratings nor the component matrices between score columns in \code{object}.
Use \code{attr(result, "summary")} to read the original estimates, sampling
variance estimates, SEs and availability. A component SE has squared score
units; the returned covariance matrix has fourth-power score units. For
a between-score covariance, the SE has the product of the two score units.
These SEs differ from the D-study's measurement SEM in original score units.

The component estimates are unchanged. This method uses Gaussian product
moments to correct plug-in bias in their estimated sampling covariance.
It does not fit a likelihood, resample data or construct confidence intervals.
In particular, \verb{Estimate +/- 1.96 * SE} is not a generally justified interval.
Use \code{\link[=confint.mfrm_multivariate_gstudy]{confint.mfrm_multivariate_gstudy()}} for its separately qualified
interval methods. A REML profile's center belongs to a different estimator;
the SE returned here describes the original ANOVA/MINQUE estimator.
